\fs36 Prayers\fs24\par
 \par
\i\fs20 For use after the Collects of Morning or Evening Prayer or separately.\par
 \par
Prayers originally composed in traditional idiom have not been\par
modernized; but, except in certain classical prayers which do not lend\par
themselves to modernization, pronouns and verbs have been put in italics\par
to assist in rendering them into contemporary speech.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl360\slmult1   \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\b Prayers for the World\b0  \par
 \par
\i 1.  For Joy in God's Creation\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O heavenly Father, \i who hast\i0  filled the world with beauty:\par
Open our eyes to behold \i thy\i0  gracious hand in all \i thy\i0  works;\par
that, rejoicing in \i thy\i0  whole creation, we may learn to serve\par
\i thee\i0  with gladness; for the sake of him through whom all\par
things were made, \i thy\i0  Son Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
  \par
\i 2.  For All Sorts and Conditions of Men\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, the creator and preserver of all mankind, we humbly\par
beseech thee for all sorts and conditions of men; that thou\par
wouldest be pleased to make thy ways known unto them, thy\par
\f1\page\f3 saving health unto all nations. More especially we pray for\par
thy holy Church universal; that it may be so guided and\par
governed by thy good Spirit, that all who profess and call\par
themselves Christians may be led into the way of truth, and\par
hold the faith in unity of spirit, in the bond of peace, and in\par
righteousness of life. Finally, we commend to thy fatherly\par
goodness all those who are in any ways afflicted or distressed,\par
in mind, body, or estate; [especially those for whom our prayers\par
are desired]; that it may please thee to comfort and relieve\par
them according to their several necessities, giving them patience\par
under their sufferings, and a happy issue out of all their\par
afflictions.  And this we beg for Jesus Christ's sake.  \i Amen.\i0\par
  \par
\i 3.  For the Human Family\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, you made us in your own image and redeemed us\par
through Jesus your Son: Look with compassion on the whole\par
human family; take away the arrogance and hatred which\par
infect our hearts; break down the walls that separate us;\par
unite us in bonds of love; and work through our struggle and\par
confusion to accomplish your purposes on earth; that, in\par
your good time, all nations and races may serve you in\par
harmony around your heavenly throne; through Jesus Christ\par
our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
  \par
\i 4.  For Peace\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 See also Various Occasions no. 18.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Eternal God, in whose perfect kingdom no sword is drawn\par
but the sword of righteousness, no strength known but the\par
strength of love: So mightily spread abroad your Spirit, that\par
all peoples may be gathered under the banner of the Prince of\par
Peace, as children of one Father; to whom be dominion and\par
glory, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\i0\par
  \par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 5.  For Peace Among the Nations\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God our heavenly Father, guide the nations of the\par
world into the way of justice and truth, and establish among\par
them that peace which is the fruit of righteousness, that they\par
may become the kingdom of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ.\par
\i Amen.\i0\par
  \par
\i 6.  For our Enemies\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, the Father of all, whose Son commanded us to love\par
our enemies: Lead them and us from prejudice to truth:\par
deliver them and us from hatred, cruelty, and revenge; and in\par
your good time enable us all to stand reconciled before you,\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
 \par
\b Prayers for the Church\b0\par
 \par
\i 7.  For the Church\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Gracious Father, we pray for thy holy Catholic Church. Fill it\par
with all truth, in all truth with all peace. Where it is corrupt,\par
purify it; where it is in error, direct it; where in any thing it is\par
amiss, reform it. Where it is right, strengthen it; where it is in\par
want, provide for it; where it is divided, reunite it; for the sake\par
of Jesus Christ thy Son our Savior.  \i Amen.\i0\par
  \par
\i 8.  For the Mission of the Church\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 See also the prayers for the Mission of the Church on pages 58, 100 and \par
101, and Various Occasions no. 16.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Everliving God, whose will it is that all should come to you\par
through your Son Jesus Christ:  Inspire our witness to him,\par
that all may know the power of his forgiveness and the hope\par
\par
\par
\f1\page\f3 of his resurrection; who lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 9.  For Clergy and People\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, from whom cometh every\par
good and perfect gift: Send down upon our bishops, and\par
other clergy, and upon the congregations committed to their\par
charge, the healthful Spirit of thy grace; and, that they may\par
truly please thee, pour upon them the continual dew of thy\par
blessing. Grant this, O Lord, for the honor of our Advocate\par
and Mediator, Jesus Christ.  \i Amen.\i0\par
  \par
\i 10.  For the Diocese\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, by your grace you have called us in this Diocese to a\par
goodly fellowship of faith. Bless our Bishop(s) \i N\i0 . [and \i N\i0 .],\par
and other clergy, and all our people. Grant that your Word\par
may be truly preached and truly heard, your Sacraments\par
faithfully administered and faithfully received. By your\par
Spirit, fashion our lives according to the example of your\par
Son, and grant that we may show the power of your love to\par
all among whom we live; through Jesus Christ our Lord.\par
\i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 11.  For the Parish\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty and everliving God, ruler of all things in heaven\par
and earth, hear our prayers for this parish family. Strengthen\par
the faithful, arouse the careless, and restore the penitent.\par
Grant us all things necessary for our common life, and bring\par
us all to be of one heart and mind within your holy Church;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 12.  For a Church Convention or Meeting\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 See also Various Occasions no. 13.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty and everliving God, source of all wisdom and\par
understanding, be present with those who take counsel\par
[in _________] for the renewal and mission of your Church.\par
Teach us in all things to seek first your honor and glory. Guide\par
us to perceive what is right, and grant us both the courage to\par
pursue it and the grace to accomplish it; through Jesus Christ\par
our Lord.  \i Amen\i0 .\par
 \par
\i 13.  For the Election of a Bishop or other Minister\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, giver of every good gift:  Look graciously on\par
your Church, and so guide the minds of those who shall\par
choose a bishop for this Diocese (\i or\i0 , rector for this parish),\par
that we may receive a faithful pastor, who will care for your\par
people and equip us for our ministries; through Jesus Christ\par
our Lord.  \i Amen\i0 .\par
 \par
\i 14.  For the Unity of the Church\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 See also Various Occasions no. 14, and Collect no. 6 (page 395).\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, our only Savior,\par
the Prince of Peace: Give us grace seriously to lay to heart the\par
great dangers we are in by our unhappy divisions; take away\par
all hatred and prejudice, and whatever else may hinder us\par
from godly union and concord; that, as there is but one Body\par
and one Spirit, one hope of our calling, one Lord, one Faith,\par
one Baptism, one God and Father of us all, so we may be all\par
of one heart and of one soul, united in one holy bond of truth\par
and peace, of faith and charity, and may with one mind and\par
one mouth glorify \i thee\i0 ; through Jesus Christ our Lord.\par
\i Amen\i0 .\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 15.  For those about to be Baptized or\par
       to renew their Baptismal Covenant\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, you prepared your disciples for the coming of the\par
Spirit through the teaching of your Son Jesus Christ: Make\par
the hearts and minds of your servants ready to receive the\par
blessing of the Holy Spirit, that they may be filled with the\par
strength of his presence; through Jesus Christ our Lord.\par
\i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 For those to be ordained, see Various Occasions no. 15.\i0\fs24  \par
 \par
\i 16.  For Monastic Orders and Vocations\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O Lord Jesus Christ, you became poor for our sake, that we\par
might be made rich through your poverty: Guide and sanctify,\par
we pray, those whom you call to follow you under the vows\par
of poverty, chastity, and obedience, that by their prayer and\par
service they may enrich your Church, and by their life and\par
worship may glorify your Name; for you reign with the Father\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\i0\par
  \par
\i 17.  For Church Musicians and Artists\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, whom saints and angels delight to worship in\par
heaven:  Be ever present with your servants who seek through\par
art and music to perfect the praises offered by your people on\par
earth; and grant to them even now glimpses of your beauty,\par
and make them worthy at length to behold it unveiled for\par
evermore; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\b\f3 Prayers for National Life\b0\par
 \par
\i 18.  For our Country\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 See also Various Occasions no. 17.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, who hast given us this good land for our\par
heritage: We humbly beseech thee that we may always prove\par
ourselves a people mindful of thy favor and glad to do thy will.\par
Bless our land with honorable industry, sound learning, and\par
pure manners.  Save us from violence, discord, and confusion;\par
from pride and arrogance, and from every evil way. Defend\par
our liberties, and fashion into one united people the multitudes brought hither out of many kindreds and tongues. Endue \par
with the spirit of wisdom those to whom in thy Name we entrust the authority of government, that there may be justice and \par
peace at home, and that, through obedience to thy law, we \par
may show forth thy praise among the nations of the earth. \par
In the time of prosperity, fill our hearts with thankfulness, \par
and in the day of trouble, suffer not our trust in thee to fail; \par
all which we ask through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
  \par
\i 19.  For the President of the United States and all in Civil\par
Authority\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O Lord our Governor, whose glory is in all the world:  We\par
commend this nation to \i thy\i0  merciful care, that, being guided\par
by \i thy\i0  Providence, we may dwell secure in \i thy\i0  peace.  Grant\par
to the President of the United States, the Governor of this\par
State (\i or\i0  Commonwealth), and to all in authority, wisdom\par
and strength to know and to do \i thy\i0  will. Fill them with the\par
love of truth and righteousness, and make them ever mindful\par
of their calling to serve this people in \i thy\i0  fear; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord, who \i liveth\i0  and \i reigneth\i0  with \i thee\i0  and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, world without end.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 20.  For Congress or a State Legislature\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, the fountain of wisdom, whose will is good and\par
gracious, and whose law is truth: We beseech \i thee\i0  so to guide\par
and bless our Senators and Representatives in Congress\par
assembled (\i or\i0  in the Legislature of this State, \i or\i0  Common-\par
wealth), that they may enact such laws as shall please \i thee\i0 ,\par
to the glory of \i thy\i0  Name and the welfare of this people;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen\i0 .\par
  \par
\i 21.  For Courts of Justice\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, \i who sittest\i0  in the throne judging right: We\par
humbly beseech \i thee\i0  to bless the courts of justice and the\par
magistrates in all this land; and give \i unto\i0  them the spirit of\par
wisdom and understanding, that they may discern the truth,\par
and impartially administer the law in the fear of \i thee\i0  alone;\par
through him who shall come to be our Judge, \i thy\i0  Son our\par
Savior Jesus Christ.  \i Amen\i0 .\par
  \par
\i 22.  For Sound Government\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 The responses in italics may be omitted.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O Lord our Governor, bless the leaders of our land, that we\par
may be a people at peace among ourselves and a blessing to\par
other nations of the earth.\par
\i Lord, keep this nation under your care.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 To the President and members of the Cabinet, to Governors\par
of States, Mayors of Cities, and to all in administrative\par
authority, grant wisdom and grace in the exercise of their\par
duties.\par
\i Give grace to your servants, O Lord.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\par
\f1\page\f3 To Senators and Representatives, and those who make our\par
laws in States, Cities, and Towns, give courage, wisdom, and\par
foresight to provide for the needs of all our people, and to\par
fulfill our obligations in the community of nations.\par
\i Give grace to your servants, O Lord\i0 .\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 To the Judges and officers of our Courts give understanding\par
and integrity, that human rights may be safeguarded and\par
justice served.\par
\i Give grace to your servants, O Lord.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 And finally, teach our people to rely on your strength and to\par
accept their responsibilities to their fellow citizens, that they\par
may elect trustworthy leaders and make wise decisions for\par
the well-being of our society; that we may serve you\par
faithfully in our generation and honor your holy Name.\par
\i For yours is the kingdom, O Lord, and you are exalted as\par
head above all.  Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 23.   For Local Government\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God our heavenly Father, send down upon those\par
who hold office in this State (Commonwealth, City, County,\par
Town, __________) the spirit of wisdom, charity, and justice;\par
that with steadfast purpose they may faithfully serve in their\par
offices to promote the well-being of all people; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 24.  For an Election\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, to whom we must account for all our powers\par
and privileges:  Guide the people of the United States (\i or\i0  of\par
this community) in the election of officials and representatives;\par
that, by faithful administration and wise laws, the rights of\par
all may be protected and our nation be enabled to fulfill your\par
purposes; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 25.  For those in the Armed Forces of our Country\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, we commend to your gracious care and\par
keeping all the men and women of our armed forces at home\par
and abroad.  Defend them day by day with your heavenly\par
grace; strengthen them in their trials and temptations; give\par
them courage to face the perils which beset them; and grant\par
them a sense of your abiding presence wherever they may be;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 26.  For those who suffer for the sake of Conscience\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God our Father, whose Son forgave his enemies while he\par
was suffering shame and death: Strengthen those who suffer\par
for the sake of conscience; when they are accused, save them\par
from speaking in hate; when they are rejected, save them\par
from bitterness; when they are imprisoned, save them from\par
despair; and to us your servants, give grace to respect their\par
witness and to discern the truth, that our society may be\par
cleansed and strengthened. This we ask for the sake of Jesus\par
Christ, our merciful and righteous Judge.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\par
\b Prayers for the Social Order\b0\par
 \par
\i 27.  For Social Justice\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 See also Various Occasions no. 21.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Grant, O God, that your holy and life-giving Spirit may so\par
move every human heart [and especially the hearts of the\par
people of this land], that barriers which divide us may\par
crumble, suspicions disappear, and hatreds cease; that our\par
divisions being healed, we may live in justice and peace;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 28.  In Times of Conflict\i0\par
 \par
O God, you have bound us together in a common life. Help us, \par
in the midst of our struggles for justice and truth, to confront \par
one another without hatred or bitterness, and to work\par
together with mutual forbearance and respect; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 29.  For Agriculture\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 See also Various Occasions no. 19.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, we thank you for making the earth fruitful, so\par
that it might produce what is needed for life: Bless those who\par
work in the fields; give us seasonable weather; and grant that\par
we may all share the fruits of the earth, rejoicing in your\par
goodness; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 For prayers for Industry and Labor, see Various Occasions no. 19,\par
no. 24, and no. 25.\i0  \fs24\par
 \par
\i 30.  For the Unemployed\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Heavenly Father, we remember before you those who suffer\par
want and anxiety from lack of work. Guide the people of this\par
land so to use our public and private wealth that all may find\par
suitable and fulfilling employment, and receive just payment\par
for their labor; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 31.  For Schools and Colleges\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O Eternal God, bless all schools, colleges, and universities\par
[and especially __________], that they may be lively centers for\par
sound learning, new discovery, and the pursuit of wisdom;\par
and grant that those who teach and those who learn may find\par
you to be the source of all truth; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3\fs20 For Education, see Various Occasions no. 23.\i0\fs24  \par
 \par
\i 32.  For the Good Use of Leisure\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, in the course of this busy life, give us times of\par
refreshment and peace; and grant that we may so use our\par
leisure to rebuild our bodies and renew our minds, that our\par
spirits may be opened to the goodness of your creation;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 33.  For Cities\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Heavenly Father, in your Word you have given us a vision of\par
that holy City to which the nations of the world bring their\par
glory: Behold and visit, we pray, the cities of the earth.\par
Renew the ties of mutual regard which form our civic life.\par
Send us honest and able leaders.  Enable us to eliminate\par
poverty, prejudice, and oppression, that peace may prevail\par
with righteousness, and justice with order, and that men and\par
women from different cultures and with differing talents may\par
find with one another the fulfillment of their humanity;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 34.  For Towns and Rural Areas\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Lord Christ, when you came among us, you proclaimed the\par
kingdom of God in villages, towns, and lonely places: Grant\par
that your presence and power may be known throughout this\par
land.  Have mercy upon all of us who live and work in rural\par
areas [especially ___________]; and grant that all the people\par
of our nation may give thanks to you for food and drink and\par
all other bodily necessities of life, respect those who labor to\par
produce them, and honor the land and the water from which\par
these good things come.  All this we ask in your holy Name.\par
\i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 35.  For the Poor and the Neglected\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty and most merciful God, we remember before you\par
all poor and neglected persons whom it would be easy for us\par
to forget:  the homeless and the destitute, the old and the sick,\par
and all who have none to care for them. Help us to heal those\par
who are broken in body or spirit, and to turn their sorrow\par
into joy. Grant this, Father, for the love of your Son, who for\par
our sake became poor, Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 36.  For the Oppressed\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Look with pity, O heavenly Father, upon the people in this\par
land who live with injustice, terror, disease, and death as\par
their constant companions.  Have mercy upon us.  Help us to\par
eliminate our cruelty to these our neighbors. Strengthen those\par
who spend their lives establishing equal protection of the law\par
and equal opportunities for all.  And grant that every one of\par
us may enjoy a fair portion of the riches of this land; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 37.  For Prisons and Correctional Institutions\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Lord Jesus, for our sake you were condemned as a criminal:\par
Visit our jails and prisons with your pity and judgment.\par
Remember all prisoners, and bring the guilty to repentance\par
and amendment of life according to your will, and give them\par
hope for their future. When any are held unjustly, bring them\par
release; forgive us, and teach us to improve our justice.\par
Remember those who work in these institutions; keep them\par
humane and compassionate; and save them from becoming\par
brutal or callous. And since what we do for those in prison,\par
O Lord, we do for you, constrain us to improve their lot. All\par
this we ask for your mercy's sake.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 38.  For the Right Use of God's Gifts\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, whose loving hand \i hath\i0  given us all that we\par
possess: Grant us grace that we may honor \i thee\i0  with our\par
substance, and, remembering the account which we must one\par
day give, may be faithful stewards of \i thy\i0  bounty, through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 39.  For those who Influence Public Opinion\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, you proclaim your truth in every age by many\par
voices: Direct, in our time, we pray, those who speak where\par
many listen and write what many read; that they may do their\par
part in making the heart of this people wise, its mind sound, and its will righteous; to the honor of Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 For Social Service, see Various Occasions no. 22\i0\fs24  \par
\pard\sl360\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\b Prayers for the Natural Order\b0\par
 \par
\i 40.  For Knowledge of God's Creation\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, you made the universe with\par
all its marvelous order, its atoms, worlds, and galaxies, and\par
the infinite complexity of living creatures: Grant that, as we\par
probe the mysteries of your creation, we may come to know\par
you more truly, and more surely fulfill our role in your\par
eternal purpose; in the name of Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 41.  For the Conservation of Natural Resources\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 See also Various Occasions no. 19.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, in giving us dominion over things on earth,\par
you made us fellow workers in your creation: Give us wisdom\par
and reverence so to use the resources of nature, that no one\par
may suffer from our abuse of them, and that generations yet\par
to come may continue to praise you for your bounty; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\par
\i\par
\i0\f1\page\i\f3 42.  For the Harvest of Lands and Waters\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O gracious Father, \i who openest thine\i0  hand and \i fillest\i0  all\par
things living with plenteousness:  Bless the lands and waters,\par
and multiply the harvests of the world; let \i thy\i0  Spirit go\par
forth, that it may renew the face of the earth; show \i thy\i0\par
loving-kindness, that our land may give her increase; and\par
save us from selfish use of what \i thou givest\i0 , that men and\par
women everywhere may give \i thee\i0  thanks; through Christ\par
our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 43.  For Rain\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1 .\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, heavenly Father, who by \i thy\i0  Son Jesus Christ\par
\i hast\i0  promised to all those who seek \i thy\i0  kingdom and its\par
righteousness all things necessary to sustain their life: Send\par
us, we entreat \i thee\i0 , in this time of need, such moderate rain\par
and showers, that we may receive the fruits of the earth, to\par
our comfort and to \i thy\i0  honor; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 44.  For the Future of the Human Race\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God our heavenly Father, you have blessed us and given us\par
dominion over all the earth: Increase our reverence before\par
the mystery of life; and give us new insight into your purposes\par
for the human race, and new wisdom and determination in\par
making provision for its future in accordance with your will;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl360\slmult1   \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\b Prayers for Family and Personal Life\b0\par
 \par
\i 45.  For Families\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, our heavenly Father, who settest the solitary\par
in families:  We commend to thy continual care the homes in\par
which thy people dwell. Put far from them, we beseech thee,\par
 \par
\f1\page\f3 every root of bitterness, the desire of vainglory, and the pride\par
of life. Fill them with faith, virtue, knowledge, temperance,\par
patience, godliness. Knit together in constant affection those\par
who, in holy wedlock, have been made one flesh. Turn the\par
hearts of the parents to the children, and the hearts of the\par
children to the parents; and so enkindle fervent charity among\par
us all, that we may evermore be kindly affectioned one\par
to another; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 A prayer for parents is on page 444.\i0\fs24  \par
 \par
\i 46.  For the Care of Children\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, heavenly Father, you have blessed us with the\par
joy and care of children: Give us calm strength and patient\par
wisdom as we bring them up, that we may teach them to love\par
whatever is just and true and good, following the example of\par
our Savior Jesus Christ.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 47.  For Young Persons\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 God our Father, you see your children growing up in an\par
unsteady and confusing world: Show them that your ways\par
give more life than the ways of the world, and that following\par
you is better than chasing after selfish goals. Help them to\par
take failure, not as a measure of their worth, but as a chance\par
for a new start. Give them strength to hold their faith in you,\par
and to keep alive their joy in your creation; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 48.  For Those Who Live Alone\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, whose Son had nowhere to lay his head:\par
Grant that those who live alone may not be lonely in their\par
solitude, but that, following in his steps, they may find\par
fulfillment in loving you and their neighbors; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 49.  For the Aged\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Look with mercy, O God our Father, on all whose increasing\par
years bring them weakness, distress, or isolation.  Provide for\par
them homes of dignity and peace; give them understanding\par
helpers, and the willingness to accept help; and, as their\par
strength diminishes, increase their faith and their assurance\par
of your love.  This we ask in the name of Jesus Christ our\par
Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 50.  For a Birthday\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, our times are in your hand:  Look with favor, we\par
pray, on your servant \i N\i0 . as \i he\i0  begins another year.  Grant\par
that \i he\i0  may grow in wisdom and grace, and strengthen \i his\i0\par
trust in your goodness all the days of \i his\i0  life; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 51.  For a Birthday\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Watch over thy child, O Lord, as \i his\i0  days increase; bless and\par
guide \i him\i0  wherever \i he\i0  may be. Strengthen \i him\i0  when \i he\i0\par
stands; comfort \i him\i0  when discouraged or sorrowful; raise\par
\i him\i0  up if \i he\i0  fall; and in \i his\i0  heart may thy peace which\par
passeth understanding abide all the days of \i his\i0  life;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 52.  For the Absent\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, whose fatherly care \i reacheth\i0  to the uttermost parts\par
of the earth: We humbly beseech \i thee\i0  graciously to behold\par
and bless those whom we love, now absent from us. Defend\par
them from all dangers of soul and body; and grant that both\par
they and we, drawing nearer to \i thee\i0 , may be bound together\par
by \i thy\i0  love in the communion of \i thy\i0  Holy Spirit, and in the\par
fellowship of \i thy\i0  saints; through Jesus Christ our Lord.\par
\i Amen.\i0\par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 53.  For Travelers\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, our heavenly Father, whose glory fills the whole\par
creation, and whose presence we find wherever we go: Preserve those who travel [in particular _____________]; surround \par
them with your loving care; protect them from every danger; and bring them in safety to their journey's end; through \par
Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen\i0 . \par
 \par
\i 54.  For those we Love\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, we entrust all who are dear to us to \i thy\i0\par
never-failing care and love, for this life and the life to come,\par
knowing that \i thou art\i0  doing for them better things than we\par
can desire or pray for; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 55.  For a Person in Trouble or Bereavement\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O merciful Father, who hast taught us in thy holy Word that\par
thou dost not willingly afflict or grieve the children of men:\par
Look with pity upon the sorrows of thy servant for whom\par
our prayers are offered. Remember \i him\i0 , O Lord, in mercy,\par
nourish \i his\i0  soul with patience, comfort \i him\i0  with a sense of\par
thy goodness, lift up thy countenance upon \i him\i0 , and give\par
\i him\i0  peace; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen\i0 .\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 Prayers for the sick are on pages 458-461. See also Various Occasions\par
no. 20.\i0\fs24\par
 \par
\i 56.  For the Victims of Addiction\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O blessed Lord, you ministered to all who came to you:  Look\par
with compassion upon all who through addiction have lost\par
their health and freedom. Restore to them the assurance of\par
your unfailing mercy; remove from them the fears that beset\par
them; strengthen them in the work of their recovery; and to\par
those who care for them, give patient understanding and\par
persevering love.  \i Amen\i0 .\par
 \par
\par
\i\par
\i0\f1\page\i\f3 57.  For Guidance\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Direct us, O Lord, in all our doings with \i thy\i0  most gracious\par
favor, and further us with \i thy\i0  continual help; that in all our\par
works begun, continued, and ended in \i thee\i0 , we may glorify\par
\i thy\i0  holy Name, and finally, by \i thy\i0  mercy, obtain everlasting\par
life; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen\i0 . \par
 \par
\i 58.  For Guidance\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, by whom the meek are guided in judgment, and\par
light \i riseth\i0  up in darkness for the godly: Grant us, in all\par
our doubts and uncertainties, the grace to ask what \i thou\par
wouldest\i0  have us to do, that the Spirit of wisdom may save\par
us from all false choices, and that in \i thy\i0  light we may see\par
light, and in \i thy\i0  straight path may not stumble; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 59.  For Quiet Confidence\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God of peace, \i who hast\i0  taught us that in returning and\par
rest we shall be saved, in quietness and in confidence shall be\par
our strength: By the might of \i thy\i0  Spirit lift us, we pray \i thee\i0 ,\par
to \i thy\i0  presence, where we may be still and know that \i thou\par
art\i0  God; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen\i0 . \par
 \par
\i 60.  For Protection\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Assist us mercifully, O Lord, in these our supplications and\par
prayers, and dispose the way of \i thy\i0  servants towards the\par
attainment of everlasting salvation; that, among all the\par
changes and chances of this mortal life, they may ever be\par
defended by \i thy\i0  gracious and ready help; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord.  \i Amen\i0 . \par
 \par
\i 61.  A Prayer of Self-Dedication\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty and eternal God, so draw our hearts to \i thee\i0 , so\par
guide our minds, so fill our imaginations, so control our\par
\f1\page\f3 wills, that we may be wholly \i thine\i0 , utterly dedicated \i unto\par
thee\i0 ; and then use us, we pray \i thee\i0 , as \i thou wilt\i0 , and always\par
to \i thy\i0  glory and the welfare of \i thy\i0  people; through our Lord\par
and Savior Jesus Christ.  \i Amen\i0 . \par
 \par
\i 62.  A Prayer attributed to St. Francis\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Lord, make us instruments of your peace. Where there is\par
hatred, let us sow love; where there is injury, pardon; where\par
there is discord, union; where there is doubt, faith; where\par
there is despair, hope; where there is darkness, light; where\par
there is sadness, joy. Grant that we may not so much seek to\par
be consoled as to console; to be understood as to understand;\par
to be loved as to love. For it is in giving that we receive; it is\par
in pardoning that we are pardoned; and it is in dying that we\par
are born to eternal life.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl360\slmult1   \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\b Other Prayers\b0\par
 \par
\pard\i\fs20 Prayers for Friday, Saturday, and Sunday, and for morning and\par
evening, are on pages 56, 69, 98, and 123.\i0  \fs24\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1  \par
\i 63.  In the Evening\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O Lord, support us all the day long, until the shadows\par
lengthen, and the evening comes, and the busy world is\par
hushed, and the fever of life is over, and our work is done.\par
Then in \i thy\i0  mercy, grant us a safe lodging, and a holy rest,\par
and peace at the last.  \i Amen\i0 . \par
 \par
\i 64.  Before Worship\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O Almighty God, \i who pourest\i0  out on all who desire it the\par
spirit of grace and of supplication:  Deliver us, when we draw\par
near to \i thee\i0 , from coldness of heart and wanderings of mind,\par
that with steadfast thoughts and kindled affections we may\par
worship \i thee\i0  in spirit and in truth; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\i\par
\i0\f1\page\i\f3 65.  For the Answering of Prayer\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, who hast promised to hear the petitions of\par
those who ask in thy Son's Name: We beseech thee mercifully\par
to incline thine ear to us who have now made our prayers and\par
supplications unto thee; and grant that those things which we\par
have faithfully asked according to thy will, may effectually be\par
obtained, to the relief of our necessity, and to the setting forth\par
of thy glory; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 66.  Before Receiving Communion\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 See also the Prayer of Humble Access on page 337.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Be present, be present, O Jesus, our great High Priest, as you\par
were present with your disciples, and be know to us in the\par
breaking of bread; who live and reign with the Father and\par
the Holy Spirit, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 67.  After Receiving Communion\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O Lord Jesus Christ, who in a wonderful Sacrament hast left\par
unto us a memorial of thy passion: Grant us, we beseech\par
thee, so to venerate the sacred mysteries of thy Body and\par
Blood, that we may ever perceive within ourselves the fruit of\par
thy redemption; who livest and reignest with the Father and\par
the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 68.  After Worship\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Grant, we beseech \i thee\i0 , Almighty God, that the words which\par
we have heard this day with our outward ears, may, through\par
\i thy\i0  grace, be so grafted inwardly in our hearts, that they may\par
bring forth in us the fruit of good living, to the honor and\par
praise of \i thy\i0  Name; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen\i0 .\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\i\f3 69.  On Sunday\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God our King, by the resurrection of your Son Jesus Christ\par
on the first day of the week, you conquered sin, put death to\par
flight, and gave us the hope of everlasting life: Redeem all\par
our days by this victory; forgive our sins, banish our fears,\par
make us bold to praise you and to do your will; and steel us\par
to wait for the consummation of your kingdom on the last\par
great Day; through the same Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 70.  Grace at Meals\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Give us grateful hearts, our Father, for all \i thy\i0  mercies, and\par
make us mindful of the needs of others; through Jesus Christ\par
our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \i\fs20\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 or this\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Bless, O Lord, \i thy\i0  gifts to our use and us to \i thy\i0  service; for\par
Christ's sake.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \i\fs20\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 or this\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Blessed are you, O Lord God, King of the Universe, for you\par
give us food to sustain our lives and make our hearts glad;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \i\fs20\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 or this\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 For these and all his mercies, God's holy Name be blessed\par
and praised; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
\fs36 Thanksgivings\fs24\par
 \par
 \par
\b General Thanksgivings\b0\par
  \par
\i 1.  A General Thanksgiving\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Accept, O Lord, our thanks and praise for all that you have\par
done for us. We thank you for the splendor of the whole\par
creation, for the beauty of this world, for the wonder of life,\par
and for the mystery of love.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 We thank you for the blessing of family and friends, and for\par
the loving care which surrounds us on every side.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 We thank you for setting us at tasks which demand our best\par
efforts, and for leading us to accomplishments which satisfy\par
and delight us.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 We thank you also for those disappointments and failures\par
that lead us to acknowledge our dependence on you alone.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Above all, we thank you for your Son Jesus Christ; for the\par
truth of his Word and the example of his life; for his steadfast\par
obedience, by which he overcame temptation; for his dying,\par
through which he overcame death; and for his rising to life\par
again, in which we are raised to the life of your kingdom.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Grant us the gift of your Spirit, that we may know him and\par
make him known; and through him, at all times and in all\par
places, may give thanks to you in all things.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 2.  A Litany of Thanksgiving\i0\par
 \par
\pard\i\fs20 For optional use on Thanksgiving Day, in place of the Prayers of the\par
People at the Eucharist, or at any time after the Collects at Morning or\par
Evening Prayer, or separately.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1  \par
\par
\f1\page\f3 Let us give thanks to God our Father for all his gifts so\par
freely bestowed upon us.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 For the beauty and wonder of your creation, in earth and\par
sky and sea,\par
\i We thank you, Lord.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 For all that is gracious in the lives of men and women,\par
revealing the image of Christ,\par
\i We thank you, Lord.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 For our daily food and drink, our homes and families, and\par
our friends,\par
\i We thank you, Lord.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 For minds to think, and hearts to love, and hands to serve,\par
\i We thank you, Lord.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 For health and strength to work, and leisure to rest and play,\par
\i We thank you, Lord.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 For the brave and courageous, who are patient in suffering\par
and faithful in adversity,\par
\i We thank you, Lord.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 For all valiant seekers after truth, liberty, and justice,\par
\i We thank you, Lord.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 For the communion of saints, in all times and places,\par
\i We thank you, Lord.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Above all, we give you thanks for the great mercies and\par
promises given to us in Christ Jesus our Lord;\par
\i To him be praise and glory, with you, O Father, and the\par
Holy Spirit, now and for ever.  Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\i\fs20 See also The General Thanksgiving on pages 58 and 101.\i0\fs24\par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\b\f3 Thanksgivings for the Church\b0\par
 \par
\i 3.  For the Mission of the Church\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, you sent your Son Jesus Christ to reconcile\par
the world to yourself: We praise and bless you for those\par
whom you have sent in the power of the Spirit to preach the\par
Gospel to all nations. We thank you that in all parts of the\par
earth a community of love has been gathered together by\par
their prayers and labors, and that in every place your servants\par
call upon your Name; for the kingdom and the power and\par
the glory are yours for ever.  \i Amen. \par
 \par
4.  For the Saints and Faithful Departed\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \i0\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 See also the prayer "O God, the King of Saints," page 489 and 504.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 We give thanks to you, O Lord our God, for all your servants\par
and witnesses of time past: for Abraham, the father of believers,\par
and Sarah his wife; for Moses, the lawgiver, and Aaron, the\par
priest; for Miriam and Joshua, Deborah and Gideon, and\par
Samuel with Hannah his mother; for Isaiah and all the prophets;\par
for Mary, the mother of our Lord; for Peter and Paul and all\par
the apostles; for Mary and Martha, and Mary Magdalene; for\par
Stephen, the first martyr, and all the martyrs and saints in\par
every age and in every land.  In your mercy, O Lord our God,\par
give us, as you gave to them, the hope of salvation and the\par
promise of eternal life; through Jesus Christ our Lord, the\par
first-born of many from the dead.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\b Thanksgivings for National Life\b0\par
 \par
\i 5.  For the Nation\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God, giver of all good things:\par
We thank you for the natural majesty and beauty of this land.\par
They restore us, though we often destroy them.\par
\i Heal us.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\par
\f1\page\f3 We thank you for the great resources of this nation. They\par
make us rich, though we often exploit them.\par
\i Forgive us.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 We thank you for the men and women who have made this\par
country strong. They are models for us, though we often fall\par
short of them.\par
\i Inspire us.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 We thank you for the torch of liberty which has been lit in\par
this land. It has drawn people from every nation, though we\par
have often hidden from its light.\par
\i Enlighten us.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 We thank you for the faith we have inherited in all its rich\par
variety. It sustains our life, though we have been faithless\par
again and again.\par
\i Renew us.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Help us, O Lord, to finish the good work here begun.\par
Strengthen our efforts to blot out ignorance and prejudice,\par
and to abolish poverty and crime. And hasten the day when\par
all our people, with many voices in one united chorus, will\par
glorify your holy Name.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 6.  For Heroic Service\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O Judge of the nations, we remember before you with grateful\par
hearts the men and women of our country who in the day of\par
decision ventured much for the liberties we now enjoy. Grant\par
that we may not rest until all the people of this land share the\par
benefits of true freedom and gladly accept its disciplines. This\par
we ask in the Name of Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
 \par
\par
\f1\page\b\f3 Thanksgiving for the Social Order\b0\par
 \par
\i 7.  For the Diversity of Races and Cultures\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 O God, who created all peoples in your image, we thank you\par
for the wonderful diversity of races and cultures in this world.\par
Enrich our lives by ever-widening circles of fellowship, and\par
show us your presence in those who differ most from us, until\par
our knowledge of your love is made perfect in our love for all\par
your children; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
 \par
\b Thanksgivings for the Natural Order\b0\par
 \par
\i 8.  For the Beauty of the Earth\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 We give you thanks, most gracious God, for the beauty of\par
earth and sky and sea; for the richness of mountains, plains,\par
and rivers; for the songs of birds and the loveliness of flowers.\par
We praise you for these good gifts, and pray that we may\par
safeguard them for our posterity. Grant that we may continue\par
to grow in our grateful enjoyment of your abundant creation,\par
to the honor and glory of your Name, now and for ever. \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 9.  For the Harvest\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Most gracious God, by whose knowledge the depths are\par
broken up and the clouds drop down the dew: We yield thee\par
hearty thanks and praise for the return of seedtime and harvest,\par
for the increase of the ground and the gathering in of its fruits,\par
and for all the other blessings of thy merciful providence\par
bestowed upon this nation and people. And, we beseech thee,\par
give us a just sense of these great mercies, such as may appear\par
in our lives by a humble, holy, and obedient walking before\par
thee all our days; through Jesus Christ our Lord, to whom,\par
with thee and the Holy Ghost be all glory and honor, world\par
without end.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
\b\par
\b0\f1\page\b\f3 Thanksgivings for Family and Personal Life\b0\par
 \par
\i 10.  For the Gift of a Child\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\i\fs20 See also the Thanksgiving for a Child on page 439.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Heavenly Father, you sent; your own Son into this world. We\par
thank you for the life of this child, \i N\i0 ., entrusted to our care.\par
Help us to remember that we are all your children, and so to\par
love and nurture \i him\i0 , that \i he\i0  may attain to that full stature\par
intended for \i him\i0  in your eternal kingdom; for the sake of\par
your dear Son, Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i 11.  For the Restoration of Health\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl204\slmult1 Almighty God and heavenly Father, we give \i thee\i0  humble\par
thanks because \i thou hast\i0  been graciously pleased to deliver\par
from \i his\i0  sickness \i thy\i0  servant \i N\i0 ., in whose behalf we bless\par
and praise \i thy\i0  Name. Grant, O gracious Father, that \i he\i0 ,\par
through \i thy\i0  help, may live in this world according to \i thy\i0  will,\par
and also be partaker of everlasting glory in the life to come;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\i\fs20 Thanksgivings for the departed are on pages 487-489 and 503-504.\i0\fs24\par
 \par
\par
}
